course: dictionary
lesson: 9624
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Stubborn» has two: it can mean a person who will not change their mind, or something that is hard to remove. The words around it show you which meaning is used.
explain: «Donkeys are not really stubborn: when something seems dangerous they stop to check instead of running.» Here stubborn is about a donkey that will not move, not about a mind. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. In «Arguments about facts are best settled by checking a trustworthy source together, not by who is more stubborn», the meaning "hard to remove" does not fit. "Not willing to change your mind" does fit, so that is the right meaning.
fact: Stubborn is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a stubborn child, a stubborn stain.
fact: «Stubborn» means not willing to change your mind or do what others want, even when you should.
fact: «Stubborn» can also mean hard to remove, move or deal with, as in «a stubborn stain» or «a stubborn cold».
fact: Its forms are stubborn, more stubborn and most stubborn.
fact: Phrases to know: «stubborn as a mule» and «a stubborn streak».
exercise: «The stubborn stain would not come out of the shirt.» What does stubborn mean here? | Very kind | *Hard to remove | Not willing to change its mind | Bright and shiny
exercise: «Kofi was stubborn and would not change his mind, even when he knew he was wrong.» What does stubborn mean here? | Hard to remove | Wet and grey | Very hungry | *Not willing to change your mind
exercise: Which phrase uses stubborn in a well-known saying? | Cold as ice | *Stubborn as a mule | Quick as a fox | Kind as a lamb
test: «Plastics are useful everywhere, but they are stubborn: they last for hundreds of years.» What does stubborn mean here? | Not willing to change | Very friendly | Loud | *Hard to get rid of
test: «When worried, a donkey tends to freeze and think rather than run, which people call stubborn.» Why do people call the donkey stubborn? | It likes the desert | It is afraid of horses | It is too hungry to move | *It will not run away when it is worried
exam: Which meaning of stubborn fits best in «Arguments about facts are best settled by checking a trustworthy source together, not by who is more stubborn»? | Hard to remove a stain | *Not willing to change your mind, even when you should | Very old | Shiny and bright
